# The rules of Towers, run with no window by domains/recreation/towers/tests/acceptance.rs: the
# real referee (recreation_towers::Game), with drones that the test puts where each step says.
# The rules do not depend on how a drone flies.

Section: The rules of Towers
  These are the rules that the game server follows, whoever commands the teams. The numbers
  are the same in a practice game in the commander app, and in the fast arena of the league.

  [[Taking a tower]] and [[Fighting for a tower]] tell you how a tower changes sides.
  [[Points and the end of the game]] tells you how to win. [[What a team sees]] tells you what
  the fog hides. [[The forest and the lanes]] and [[Flying low]] tell you what the trees do.
  [[Radio shadows]] tells you how a tower blocks the radio of the enemy. [[Kinds of tower]] tells you how a fort, a spire and a depot differ. [[Standing orders]] tell
  you what a drone does when it is out of contact. [[The mountains]] tells
  you what stands at the edge of the field.
  [[The computer commander]] tells you how the computer plays a team.

